    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWell, I have mapped K to vim.lsp.buf.hover() so when ever I do press K the hover pops normally. But on small screens and specially when it is large & wrapped commenting over the hovered item it becomes impossible to scroll the doc without a mouse. \n\nThis forces me to press K again to get into the window and the result is that the native markdown rendering vanishes.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI am not sure whether vim.lsp.buf.hover() has a dedicated event or not but I want it to have a minimal one so that we can safely map keys like `<C-f>` , `<C-b>` for scrolling during the valid Event time.\n\nI know that would be an overkill but since hover() is a special feature so it deserves a speical Event for safer mapping.\n\nThe core motive is to apply scrolling to vim.lsp.buf.hover() through some certain non conflicting keys.\n\nI dislike using mouse and have disabled it in config so it will be a better idea to discard this issue at first sight rather than suggesting me that thing.\n\nForgive me if there was any mistake in the issue.",
