        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Yes, but you should explain what exactly \"destroys the markdown rendering\" means?\n\nNeovim has a default markdown rendering for hover docs so whenever we do K(default map) followed by another K in normal mode we get our cursor inside the Hover.\n\nBut this makes the .md lose rendering where the cursor lands on a link/ block as by default neovim expands the underlying value to to the user for more information. \n\nThis reduces focus while reading and exploring.\n\n",
